<!--
  Static, hand-maintained — the marketing route set is small and fixed
  today, so a build-time generator would be pure overhead. Lists only
  canonical, public, indexable pages: no login/registration flows, no
  authenticated app routes, no per-customer or per-delivery pages.
  /status is deliberately omitted — it's marked noindex (see
  src/lib/seo/page-head.ts), so it shouldn't appear in a sitemap either.

  Future: public vendor storefronts (/store/:slug) are intentionally
  crawlable (see public/robots-marketing.txt) but are NOT listed here —
  there is no per-vendor sitemap generation yet. When storefronts are
  ready to be actively promoted in search, add a build- or request-time
  job that lists active, publicly-visible vendor slugs (companies with
  commerce_enabled and a published storefront) and either appends them
  here or serves a separate /sitemap-stores.xml referenced from a
  sitemap index — do not hand-maintain that list.
-->
